# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# CITATION.cff — GitHub reads this from the ROOT of the default branch only.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this game or its reference implementation in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Airborne Submarine Squadron"
type: software
version: "0.5.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/hyperpolymath/airborne-submarine-squadron"
abstract: >-
  A Sopwith-style arcade game in which the aircraft is also a submarine that can dive, fly, and leave the
  atmosphere for orbit. A fixed-timestep deterministic JavaScript engine with an AffineScript/typed-WASM core
  in progress; a worked example of reproducible, replayable, verifiable game simulation.
keywords: [game, sopwith, arcade, deterministic-simulation, webassembly, affinescript, fixed-timestep]
authors:
  - family-names: Jewell
    given-names: "Jonathan D.A."
    email: "j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk"
    alias: hyperpolymath
  - family-names: Jewell
    given-names: Joshua
    alias: JoshuaJewell
